eneric:\n    - text: Agronomic Roadmap\n    - heading \"Seasonal Farming Calendar & Practices Guide\" [level=2]\n    - text: Comprehensive month-by-month agricultural operations, crop sowing windows, and agronomic management for maximum crop resilience.\n    - button \"Print / Save Seasonal Checklist\" [ref=e30] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - button \"All Seasons\" [ref=e31] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - button \"Kharif (Monsoon)\" [ref=e32] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - button \"Rabi (Winter)\" [ref=e33] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - button \"Zaid (Summer)\" [ref=e34] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - generic:\n      - text: June to October · Paddy, Maize, Cotton, Soybean, Groundnut, Pulses (Arhar/Moong)\n      - heading \"Kharif Season (Monsoon / Summer Sowing)\" [level=3]\n      - generic:\n        - text: May - June\n        - heading \"Land Preparation\" [level=4]\n        - text: Deep summer plowing to expose pest pupae to sunlight. Clean drainage ditches to prevent flash flooding.\n        - generic [ref=e101] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [checked] [ref=e102] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: June - July\n        - heading \"Sowing & Nursery\" [level=4]\n        - text: Transplant rice seedlings at 21-25 days age. Inoculate legume seeds with Rhizobium culture.\n        - generic [ref=e103] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e104] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: July - August\n        - heading \"Irrigation & Nutrients\" [level=4]\n        - text: Maintain 3-5 cm standing water in paddy fields. Apply 1st top dressing of Nitrogen during active tillering.\n        - generic [ref=e105] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e106] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: September - October\n        - heading \"Harvest & Post-Harvest\" [level=4]\n        - text: Drain field 10 days before harvest. Cut crop when 85% grains turn golden; dry to 12% moisture.\n        - generic [ref=e107] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e108] [offscreen]\n      - text: Agronomist's Golden Rule · Do not allow stagnant water in maize and pulse fields during peak monsoon spells.\n    - generic:\n      - text: October to April · Wheat, Mustard, Barley, Chickpea, Potato, Tomato, Peas\n      - heading \"Rabi Season (Winter / Spring Harvest)\" [level=3]\n      - generic:\n        - text: October - November\n        - heading \"Land Preparation\" [level=4]\n        - text: Incorporate crop residue with rotavator. Apply basal doses of Phosphorus, Potash, and Sulfur.\n        - generic [ref=e109] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e110] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: November\n        - heading \"Sowing & Nursery\" [level=4]\n        - text: \"Optimal wheat sowing window: Nov 10 to Nov 25. Sow treated seeds with seed-cum-fertilizer drill.\"\n        - generic [ref=e111] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e112] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: December - February\n        - heading \"Irrigation & Nutrients\" [level=4]\n        - text: 1st wheat irrigation at CRI (21 days) is critical. Watch for Yellow Rust in January foggy days.\n        - generic [ref=e113] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e114] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: March - April\n        - heading \"Harvest & Post-Harvest\" [level=4]\n        - text: Harvest wheat and mustard in early morning to prevent pod shattering. Store grains under 11% moisture.\n        - generic [ref=e115] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e116] [offscreen]\n      - text: Agronomist's Golden Rule · Never miss the 1st irrigation in wheat at 21 days (Crown Root Initiation stage).\n    - generic:\n      - text: March to June · Watermelon, Muskmelon, Cucumber, Okra (Bhindi), Moong (Green Gram), Fodder Cowpea\n      - heading \"Zaid Season (Short Summer / Pre-Monsoon)\" [level=3]\n      - generic:\n        - text: February - March\n        - heading \"Land Preparation\" [level=4]\n        - text: Prepare high raised beds or pits with enriched vermicompost for cucurbit vines.\n        - generic [ref=e117] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e118] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: March\n        - heading \"Sowing & Nursery\" [level=4]\n        - text: Sow seeds in warm soil with plastic mulch to conserve precious soil moisture and suppress weeds.\n        - generic [ref=e119] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e120] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: April - May\n        - heading \"Irrigation & Nutrients\" [level=4]\n        - text: Frequent light drip irrigations every 3-4 days during peak summer heat to prevent fruit dropping.\n        - generic [ref=e121] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e122] [offscreen]\n      - generic:\n        - text: May - June\n        - heading \"Harvest & Post-Harvest\" [level=4]\n        - text: Harvest melons when ground spot turns creamy yellow and tendril withers; harvest early morning.\n        - generic [ref=e123] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n          - checkbox \"Completed in Field\" [ref=e124] [offscreen]\n      - text: Agronomist's Golden Rule · Growing short-duration summer Moong enriches soil with 30-40 kg natural atmospheric nitrogen for the upcoming paddy.\n  - generic:\n    - text: Pathology Diagnostic AI\n    - heading \"Crop Doctor & Pest/Disease Diagnostic Tool\" [level=2]\n    - text: Identify plant illnesses, fungal blights, and insect infestations quickly. Get certified organic remedies and recommended chemical treatments. · Field Symptom Checklist\n    - button \"Clear Selection\" [ref=e59] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - generic:\n      - text: 1. Select Affected Crop\n      - button \"Tomato\" [ref=e60] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Rice\" [ref=e61] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Wheat\" [ref=e62] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Potato\" [ref=e63] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Mustard\" [ref=e64] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - generic:\n      - text: 2. Plant Part Showing Symptoms\n      - button \"Leaf\" [ref=e65] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Stem\" [ref=e66] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Fruit\" [ref=e67] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - generic:\n      - text: 3. Observable Symptoms\n      - button \"Yellowing / Chlorosis\" [ref=e125] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Brown / Black Spots\" [ref=e126] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Wilting / Drooping\" [ref=e70] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Leaf Curling / Cupping\" [ref=e71] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n      - button \"Stunted Bushy Growth\" [ref=e72] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - generic:\n      - text: Or select a real field leaf sample\n      - button [ref=e73] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n        - img \"Early Blight (Alternaria solani)\"\n        - text: Tomato\n      - button [ref=e74] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n        - img \"Rice Blast (Magnaporthe oryzae)\"\n        - text: Rice / Paddy\n      - button [ref=e75] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n        - img \"Yellow Stripe Rust (Puccinia striiformis)\"\n        - text: Wheat\n      - generic [ref=e76] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]:\n        - button \"Upload Leaf Photo / Camera\" [ref=e77] [offscreen]\n    - button \"Analyze Symptoms & Diagnose\" [ref=e78] [cursor=pointer] [offscreen]\n    - text: Agronomic Diagnostic Report · 94% Confidence Match · Severe (Immediate Intervention)\n    - heading \"Rice Blast (Magnaporthe oryzae)\" [level=3]\n    - text: Spindle-shaped elliptical lesions with grayish centers and dark brown margins. · Organic & Bio-Remedy · Spray fermented cow urine extract (10%) with turmeric powder or Pseudomonas fluorescens (5g/L). · Scientific Chemical Treatment · Tricyclazole 75% WP @ 0.6 g/L or Isoprothiolane 40% EC @ 1.5 ml/L at first appearance of spots. · Long-Term Preventive Measures · Avoid excessive urea/nitrogen applications which make foliage soft and succulent to fungal spores. · Always wear safety gloves and follow recommended pre-harvest intervals (PHI) when applying chemical sprays.\n  - generic:\n    - text: Market Intelligence\n    - heading \"Live Mandi Commodity Rates & MSP Tracker\" [level=2]\n    - text: Compare daily Mandi arrival prices with the Government Minimum Support Price (MSP) to make informed selling decisions.\n    - textbox \"Filter by crop, state, or market mandi...\" [ref=e79] [offscreen]\n    - table:\n      - row:\n        - columnheader \"Crop / Commodity\"\n        - columnheader \"Mandi Market (State)\"\n        - columnheader \"Govt MSP (₹/Qtl)\"\n        - columnheader \"Modal Price (₹/Qtl)\"\n        - columnheader \"Daily Trend\"\n        - columnheader \"Arrivals\"\n      - row: Wheat (Sharbati/Mill Quality) · FAQ / Sharbati · Khanna Mandi, Punjab · ₹ · 2,275 · ₹ · 2,480 · +2.8% · 4,250 Qtl\n      - row: Paddy (Basmati 1509) · Basmati Super · Karnal Mandi, Haryana · ₹ · 2,300 · ₹ · 3,450 · +4.1% · 8,900 Qtl\n      - row: Mustard Seed · Black Mustard (Bold) · Bharatpur Mandi, Rajasthan · ₹ · 5,650 · ₹ · 5,920 · +1.9% · 3,120 Qtl\n      - row: Gram / Chickpea (Desi) · Desi Medium · Indore Mandi, Madhya Pradesh · ₹ · 5,440 · ₹ · 5,850 · +1.2% · 2,400 Qtl\n      - row: Potato (Jyoti / Kufri) · Table Grade · Agra Mandi, Uttar Pradesh · ₹ · 1,100 · ₹ · 1,540 · -1.5% · 14,500 Qtl\n      - row: Hybrid Tomato · Red Firm Ripe · Pimpalgaon Mandi, Nashik · ₹ · 1,200 · ₹ · 2,100 · +6.5% · 6,800 Crates\n      - row: Maize / Corn · Yellow Feed Grade · Gulabbagh Mandi, Bihar · ₹ · 2,090 · ₹ · 2,280 · +0.8% · 5,300 Qtl\n      - row: CTC Tea (Dust / Fannings) · BOP / Dust Grade · Guwahati Tea Auction Centre, Assam · ₹ · 180 · ₹ · 245 · +3.4% · 32,000 Pkgs\n    - text: Welfare & Grants\n    - heading \"Agricultural Welfare Schemes & Subsidies\" [level=2]\n    - text: Verified financial support, crop insurance, and solar mechanization programs for Indian farmers.\n    - generic:\n      - text: Direct Income Support\n      - heading \"PM-KISAN (Pradhan Mantri Kisan Samman Nidhi)\" [level=3]\n      - text: \"Financial / Equipment Benefit : · ₹6,000 per year directly credited into farmer bank accounts in three equal 4-monthly installments of ₹2,000. · Eligibility Criteria : · All landholding farmer families with cultivable land in their names. Aadhar-seeded active bank account and eKYC completed.\"\n      - button \"View Application Steps\" [ref=e80] [cursor=pointer] [occluded]\n    - generic:\n      - text: Comprehensive Crop Insurance\n      - heading \"PMFBY (Pradhan Mantri Fasal Bima Yojana)\" [level=3]\n      - text: \"Financial / Equipment Benefit : · Comprehensive risk insurance covering yield losses due to non-preventable natural risks (drought, flood, hailstorm, pests). Farmer pays only 2% for Kharif, 1.5% for Rabi. · Eligibility Criteria : · All farmers growing notified crops in notified areas including sharecroppers and tenant farmers.\"\n      - button \"View Application Steps\" [ref=e81] [cursor=pointer] [occluded]\n    - generic:\n      - text: Up to 60% Solar Subsidy\n      - heading \"PM-KUSUM (Solar Agri Pump & Grid Subsidy)\" [level=3]\n      - text: \"Financial / Equipment Benefit : · Government subsidy of up to 60% for installing standalone solar agriculture pumps (3HP to 7.5HP) and solarizing existing grid-connected electric pumps. · Eligibility Criteria : · Farmers with agricultural land possessing an existing borewell/well requiring irrigation.\"\n      - 